{
  "id": "VA-HB-904-2024",
  "scope": "state:va",
  "title": "HB 904 (2024 Regular Session (LIS session code 241)): Voter registration; list maintenance activities, cancellation procedures, required record matches.",
  "urls": [
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+sum+HB904",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+mbr+HB904",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+ful+HB904ER",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+ful+HB904 (introduced; not read)",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+ful+HB904H1 (House committee substitute; not read)"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship)\n(section) § 24.2-427 B (as passed (enrolled; struck words removed, new words kept))\n(quote) B. Upon receipt of a report from the Department of Motor Vehicles pursuant to § 24.2-410.1 or from the Department of Elections based on information received from the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements Program (SAVE Program) pursuant to subsection E of § 24.2-404, the general registrar shall mail notice promptly to all persons listed in the report as not being a citizen of the United States prior to cancelling the registrations of such persons. The notice shall inform the person of the report from the Department of Motor Vehicles or from the Department of Elections and allow the person to submit his sworn statement that he is a United States citizen within 14 days of the date that the notice was mailed. The general registrar shall cancel the registrations of such persons who do not respond within 14 days to the notice that they have been reported not to be United States citizens.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) § 24.2-410.3 C (as passed (enrolled; struck words removed, new words kept))\n(quote) C. The Department shall not utilize any data received pursuant to subsection A for list maintenance purposes when such data file does not include a unique identifier for each individual whose information is contained in the data file. For purposes of this subsection, a \"unique identifier\" means an individual's full social security number or Virginia Department of Motor Vehicles customer identifier number, or any data field or combination of data fields that can be reliably linked to a single individual.\n(other) § 2.2-3711: closed meetings\n(other) §§ 24.2-404, 24.2-407.2, 24.2-407.3: system security, list maintenance and record-match standards (point values for SSN and other matches); §§ 24.2-410.3 to 24.2-410.6: exchange of voter lists with other states, regular periodic review, inactive status, cancellation after inactivity\n(other) §§ 24.2-408, 24.2-409, 24.2-410, 24.2-410.1: identification fields required on death, felony, incapacity and DMV lists\n(other) §§ 24.2-426.1, 24.2-427: cancellation of registration; §§ 24.2-428 to 24.2-428.2 repealed\n(other) § 24.2-435, 24.2-444: records\n(other) § 24.2-703.1: permanent absentee voter list\n(other) Repeals §§ 24.2-404.3, 24.2-404.4, 24.2-410.2\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
  "sponsors": [
